Z||000000||gdogg||03-09-2000||06:26 AM||||I got a racing ticket jan 1st with my 1990 chevy beretta 3.1L, but got it reduced to speeding over 25 (on tuesday). I got my Fiero a couple days after I got the ticket and the police will slow down just to let me pass them. Its got me paranoid. Anyone else have this experience? <P>There are about four other fieros around here in hunstville, Al (that i've seen). One is Purplish and very nice. Does anyone that posts on here live near huntsville?<BR>||||reg||8
Z||000001||DJRice||03-09-2000||08:50 AM||||The police slow down so you will pass them so they can check your tag and sticker.  It seems to be standard operating procedure.  <P>That having been said, it couldnt hurt to use some better judgement about where you put the pedal down  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||william_thorniii||03-09-2000||11:52 AM||||gdogg,<P>You are near the Mecca of Fiero-dom.  Ed Parks runs "The Fiero Factory" in Toney, AL.  There is a member here witht the screen name "Cooter" that isn't too far from you.  You can also find the Michigan Fiero Club web page and search through F.O.L.D.  (Fiero Owners Location Database).  It should give you a list of many Fiero owners in your area.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
